% Isomap aims to recover the intrinsic geometric structure of the manifold by preserving geodesic distances between all pairs of data points. LLE \cite{roweis2000nonlinear} is an unsupervised learning algorithm that computes low-dimensional, neighborhood-preserving embeddings of high-dimensional inputs. What makes LLE different from the clustering algorithms is that LLE maps its inputs into a single global coordinate system of lower dimensionality, and its optimizations do not involve local minima. By using the local symmetries of linear reconstructions, LLE can learn the global structure of nonlinear manifolds. Laplacian eigenmaps (LE) \cite{belkin2003laplacian} is also used to find out low dimensional data lying in a very high-dimensional space. Principal component analysis (PCA) \cite{vidal2016principal}, is a dimensionality reduction method that is often used to reduce the dimensionality of large data sets, by transforming a large set of variables into a smaller one that still contains most of the information in the large set but its effectiveness is limited by its global linearity.
