\section{Level valuations}

Let $\star \in \{ \mKT, \mKTB, \mKTfor, \mKTBfourfive \}$. 

\begin{definition}[Valuation function]
    The valuation in $\mathcal{M}_{\star}$ is a function $v : For(\star) \to \mathcal{V}$ such that 

    \[
        v(\# (\alpha_0, \ldots, \alpha_n)) \in \#^{\star}(v(\alpha_0), \ldots, v(\alpha_n))
    \]

    with $\# \in \{ \neg, \to, \land, \lor, \Box, \Diamond \}$.

\end{definition}


The first level\co{Not clear to me... at the atomic level?} (level $0$) is the set of every valuation function in $\mathcal{M}_{\star}$:

\[
\mathcal{L}_0 = Val(\mathcal{M}_{\star})
\]

The level $k+1$ is defined as follows:

\[
\mathcal{L}_{k+1} = \{ v \in \mathcal{L}_{k} \mid \forall A, \text{ if } \Vdash^{\mathcal{L}_k}_{\mathcal{M}_{\star}} A, \text{ then }  v(\Box A) \in \mathcal{D}\}
\]

The set of level valuations is thus defined as the intersection of every level:

\[
\mathcal{L} = \bigcap^{\infty}_{k = 0} L_k
\]

In what follows, we denote the consequence relation in the corresponding axiomatic system as $\vdash_{\star}$. The notation $\vdash_{\star^{-}}$ refers to the consequence relation of the modal system without the Rule of Necessitation. Additionally, $\Vdash_{\mathcal{M}_{\star}}$ represents the semantic consequence relation in the nmatrix for $\star$, while $\Vdash_{\mathcal{M}_{\star}}^{\mathcal{L}}$ indicates the semantic consequence relation in the nmatrix for $\star$ with level valuations.

