        \item If $v_p(\alpha) = \fcont$, then there is a level valuation $w$ in $\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M}_{\mKTBfourfive})$ such that $\tilde w^{\star}(\alpha) \in \{ \tnec, \tcont \}$ and, $\forall \beta \in \Lambda$, $v_p(\beta) = \tnec$ if, and only if, $w(\beta) = \tnec$.
        \item If $v_p(\alpha) = \tcont$, then there is a level valuation $w$ in $\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{M}_{\mKTBfourfive})$ such that $\tilde w^{\star}(\alpha) \in \{ \fnec, \fcont \}$ and, $\forall \beta \in \Lambda$, $v_p(\beta) = \tnec$ if, and only if, $w(\beta) = \tnec$.
