\section{Translating Weak Alternating Automata to COCOA}\label{sec:WAA-to-COCOA}
This section describes our main result: a translation from weak alternating B\"uchi automata to COCOA.
Section~\ref{sec:obligation-graphs} defines \emph{obligation graphs},
which are the nondeterministic B\"uchi automata resulting from applying the Miyano-Hayashi's construction to the dual of input weak alternating automata.
Based on obligation graphs,
Section~\ref{sec:SLTM} defines \emph{suffix-language-tracking machines}:
these machines track the suffix language of our language after reading a finite prefix word.
With the aid of the suffix machine, we then saturate the set of initial vertices of the obligation graph.
After these preparations,
Section~\ref{subsec:Al} describes the construction of level automata $\mc A^\ell$ of COCOA.

\subsection{Obligation graphs}
\label{sec:obligation-graphs}
Given a weak alternating Büchi automaton $\mc A = (\Sigma, Q, q_0, \delta,F)$,
its \emph{obligation graph} is an NBW $\mc G = (\Sigma, V, V_0, \delta^\mc G,F_\mc G)$
resulting from applying the Miyano-Hayashi's construction to $\bar {\mc A}$.
Thus, $L(\mc G) = \overline{L(\mc A)}$.

