Later, we will use the following properties P1--P4 of canonical SLTMs,
where properties P1--P3 follow easily from the definitions and P4 follows from the way we constructed the canonical SLTM in the proof of Lemma~\ref{lem:canonical-SLTM}\ak{i wonder if it can be proven directly from the def}.
\lo[P1.]
\-\label{SLTM:P1}
  For every state $q^S$ of $\mc M$ and $v \in q^S$,
  there exists a prefix $p$: $v_0 \stackrel{p}{\rightsquigarrow} v \textit{ and } L^\textit{suff}(p) = \lambda(q^S)$.
\-\label{SLTM:P2}
  For every
  prefix word $p$,
  $v$ s.t.\ $v_0 \stackrel{p}{\rightsquigarrow} v$, and
  $q^S$ s.t.\ $q_0^S \stackrel{p}{\rightsquigarrow} q^S$:~
  $q^S$ contains $v$.
