[1] Assume that $c_L\neq B$. This implies that $\tilde{q}$ has the form $(q,d)$.

(a) We first consider the case where $depth(a)\leq k-2$ and $d'=+1$. Since $\tilde{a}=[\setempty,a,T_v]$, $N$ writes $[\setempty,b,T_v]$ over $\tilde{a}$. Let $(s,d'')$ denote $D_{\delta}(\setempty\mmid p,+1\mmid T_v)$. We then force $N$ to enter $(T_v,s,d'')$ from $\tilde{q}$. For the tape head direction, if $d''=+1$, then $N$ moves to the right; however, if $d''=-1$, then $N$ makes a storage stationary move.
In the next case where $depth(a)\leq k-3$ and $d'=-1$, nevertheless, we force $N$ to write $[\setempty,b,T_v]$ over $[\setempty,a,T_v]$ and to make a left turn by changing $\tilde{q}$ to $(p,-1)$.

