In the case where $depth(a)=k-1$ and $d'=+1$, $N$ also writes $B$ over $\tilde{a}$ and changes $\tilde{q}$ to $(T_{wB},p,+1)$.

[2] Opposite to [1], we assume that $c_L=B$, implying that $\tilde{q}$ has the form $(T_w,q,d)$.

