If $d''=+1$, then $N$ moves to the right. In contrast, if $d''=-1$, then $N$ makes a storage stationary move because the current tape cell is a left fringe of a blank region and $N$'s storage-tape head returns to this fringe after entering this blank region.
In the case where $depth(a)\leq k-3$ and $d'=-1$, $N$ writes $[T_w,b,T_v]$ over $\tilde{a}$. If $(s,d'')$ expresses the outcome of $D_{\delta}(T_w\mmid p,-1\mmid \setempty)$, then $N$ enters inner state $(T_w,s,d'')$. Moreover, when  $d''=+1$, $N$ makes a storage stationary move and, when $d''=-1$, by contrast, $N$ makes a left turn.

