\subsection{Proof of Lemma \ref{aux-sna-to-circuit}}\label{sec:lemma-proof}

In Section \ref{sec:simulation}, we have proven Theorem   \ref{circuit-character} with the help of two supporting lemmas, Lemmas \ref{aux-sna-to-circuit} and \ref{circuit-to-aux-sna}.
This subsection provides the missing proof of Lemma  \ref{aux-sna-to-circuit}.
To begin with the actual proof, let us focus on a weakly depth-susceptible  aux-$k$-sna $M$ with runtime bound $t(n)$ and work space bound $s(n)$ and assume that $M$ is right-turn restricted and makes no frozen blank turn on all inputs.
Recall from Section \ref{sec:useful} a tree-like structure, which represents a computation path of $M$ on input $x$. By Lemma \ref{tree-like-realizable}, it suffices to ``describe'' such a tree-like structure using an appropriate logspace-uniform family $\CC=\{G_n\}_{n\in\nat}$ of $k$-cascading circuits.

