Our profiling results yield two key observations: \textbf{First}, the rendering process on edge devices is predominantly memory bandwidth-bound. The proportion of time spent on memory access in edge computing platforms is $4.79\times \sim 5.14\times$ higher than in high-end computing platforms, due to the smaller L2 cache size and relatively low DRAM bandwidth of edge devices. \textbf{Second}, there is substantial redundancy in voxel grid data. 
