These discriminative features are useful for multiple tasks. For classification,~\cite{mukhopadhyay2023diffusion} explores feature extraction and shows how diffusion models are stronger than other generative models on discriminative tasks. There has also been significant exploration on using diffusion models as encoders for segmentation tasks~\cite{xu2023odise, karazija2023diffusion}. Particularly~\cite{xu2023odise} shows how diffusion models have both strong open vocabulary and region-level understanding by achieving SoTA performance using a frozen diffusion backbone. Finally,~\cite{he2023discffusion} explains that diffusion models can achieve state-of-the-art on few-shot image-text matching. Following a similar strategy to these papers, we show how diffusion models can provide sufficiently strong discriminative features for visual instruction tuning.

