\subsection{Hardware deliverables of IP protectable assets}
The deliverables of a typical hardware project can be: the layout ready to tape-out to a ASIC vendor (e.g. TSMC, XFAB, or GF); the P \&R (place and route) project ready to be imported into a ASIC vendor tool (e.g. the GDSII file); the schematic or netlist in some vendor tool format (i.e. Cadence, Mentor). The outcome of a hardware project can also be a set of Gerber files for a PCB layout.
For an RTL project, Verilog or VHDL files are the foundation of the project (although higher level languages as SystemVerilog, SystemC or Chisel are getting more importance), but intermediate files as netlist (EDIF format) or final files as bitstreams can also be the outcomes of the project.

