    Note that although word-to-word $\MSOSI$ have both the \FO and the \FOC backward translation property, these properties hold for quite different reasons, and this has consequences. Firstly, the \FO backward translation property holds for arbitrary structures, whereas one needs a suitable automaton model to obtain the same property for \FOC. Moreover, in the case of \FO, this is obtained via simple formula substitutions, yet it is much more involved when adding counting quantifiers.
\end{remark}
