\emph{Closure under \square} We refer the reader to Example~\ref{ex:square}
for a definition of the transduction $\square$. Let $f\in \LEX$. If $f$ is simple, then it is
immediate that $(\square\ f)\in \SEQ$ and the result follows from
Lemma~\ref{lem:seqlex}. Otherwise, assume
