    (3)$\Rightarrow$ (2) Mealy machines compute particular cases of polyregular transductions.

    (2)$\Rightarrow$ (3) For this direction we rely on several decomposition results. The first, from \cite[Lemma~9]{BKL19} says that any polyregular transduction can be obtained as the composition of a first-order interpretation and a rational letter-to-letter transduction.
    Secondly, rational transductions are known to be compositions of sequential and co-sequential transductions \cite{DBLP:books/lib/Berstel79}. Moreover, a co-sequential function is the composition of the form $\rev\circ f\circ \rev$ with $f$ sequential, and $\rev$ is an \FOI.
