\begin{thm}\normalsize\label{thm:arac2009}
  Let $f$ be a BAN, with $G_f = (V, E)$ its associated interaction graph. 
  Let $s_1$ and $s_2$ be two distinct block-sequential update modes defined on $V$, and 
  $(G_f, \text{lab}_{s_1})$ 
  and $(G_f, \text{lab}_{s_2})$ their related update digraphs. 
  The following result holds: if $(G_f, \text{lab}_{s_1}) = (G_f, \text{lab}_{s_2})$, then the 
  dynamics of $f$ under $s_1$ is exactly the same as that of $f$ under $s_2$.
\end{thm}

