Plants are naturally attuned to their environments, capable of sensing changes in air quality ~\cite{matthen2024plants, napier2023gene, demey2023sound}, temperature ~\cite{kerbler2023temperature}, presence of specific airborne chemicals or pollutants ~\cite{hong2023plants, matsui2016portion}, and even presence of human ~\cite{de2023can}.
